{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/manifests/portal-fantasy-a-case-study-of-narnia.json","type":"Manifest","label":{"en":["Portal Fantasy: A Case Study of Narnia"]},"homepage":[{"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling","type":"Text","label":{"en":["Portal Fantasy: A Case Study of Narnia"]},"format":"text/html"}],"metadata":[{"label":{"en":["Description"]},"value":{"en":["Annotations by Bridie Pickering"]}},{"label":{"en":["Language"]},"value":{"en":["English"]}}],"items":[{"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3","type":"Canvas","duration":215,"annotations":[{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/manifests/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia-canvas3-1","type":"AnnotationPage","label":{"en":["Default"]},"items":[{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"The way Lucy moves backwards into the wardrobe seems like she's playing hide and seek. She doesn't expect anything to be behind her but more clothes. She's hiding in a wardrobe, a very mundane place for a child to hide. ","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Worldbuilding","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Portal Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Magic System","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3#t=0,22"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"She slowly turns around to investigate why she felt the cold of snow on her fingertips, and then quickly looks back, to make sure no one is following her. It's almost like she doesn't want to get into trouble for going somewhere she isn't supposed to go. ","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Worldbuilding","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Portal Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Rules","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3#t=23,32"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Lucy is completely enthralled by the winter wonderland she's found through the doorway in the wardrobe. She can't believe that it was waiting for her, hiding in a wardrobe, of all things. She has found the portal to Narnia.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Worldbuilding","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Magic System","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Portal Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3#t=33,75"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"She glances over her shoulder quickly, to make sure that she can still return home. She wants to explore the new world, but she doesn't want to leave her life behind either. As long as the portal is there, Lucy could have Narnia, and her world, too. ","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Worldbuilding","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Magic System","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Portal Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3#t=76,85"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"The inclusion of the lamppost is a hilarious detail by CS Lewis, because he and Tolkien had an argument that including things like a lamppost would break immersion for the reader, because then they would wonder how electricity existed in a magical world, who put it there, or where it came from. CS Lewis did it to spite Tolkien. ","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Portal Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Worldbuilding","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Magic System","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3#t=86,120"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Lucy's encounter with the fawn frightens them both. Lucy is confused because it's not human, and this is the first moment where she has seen something outside of the ordinary in Narnia. This is when she begins to learn she's stepped through a portal into another world.\nIn order to communicate that Lucy is in a magical world, they need to establish that there are normal things (trees, snow, lampposts) in this magical world, but also fawns and mythical creatures.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Magic System","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Worldbuilding","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Portal Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3#t=121,150"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Lucy's curiosity quickly gets the better of her fear, and she approaches the fawn, eager to explore this magical world she's discovered. Though she doesn't know if she's safe, it's like she thinks a world this magical couldn't possibly put her in danger.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Worldbuilding","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Rules","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Magic System","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Portal Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3#t=151,180"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Lucy is careful when she interacts with the world around her. She struggles to believe the fawn would be frightened of her, and is put at ease when he says he didn't want to frighten Lucy. It makes her feel safe in Narnia.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Portal Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Worldbuilding","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Rules","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Magic System","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3#t=181,215"}]},{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/manifests/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia-canvas3-1","type":"AnnotationPage","label":{"en":["Default"]},"items":[]}],"items":[{"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia-canvas3/paintings","type":"AnnotationPage","items":[{"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia-canvas3/paintings","type":"Annotation","motivation":"painting","body":{"id":"https://youtu.be/FqXeJpy0gkQ?si=KQMzZAztvDhe7eAV","type":"Video","format":"unknown","duration":215},"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/portal_fantasy_a_case_study_of_narnia/canvas/3"}]}]}]}